// Questions whose useful answer sits on an entity NOTHING connects to the one
// asked about -- no edge, no shared words, only a value the two happen to hold in
// common. This suite is what justifies the kin channel over the graph channel.
//
// The shapes are taken from a production brain, with its names replaced: that
// brain had 59 of 69 `is_a` facts stored as strings, so several cases here record
// a class as text rather than as an edge. A channel that only worked on
// well-formed brains would not have helped the brain that needed it.
//
// A parallel recollection is not supposed to beat the answer the question
// actually asked for: when the query names an entity, that entity's own facts are
// the right top hit and the kin fact belongs just below. Cases of that shape
// therefore expect both. The two that ask for a property the anchor does not have
// are the exception -- there the lateral fact is the only answer there is.
//
// What the numbers turned out to say: R@5 and R@10 do not move when the channel
// is switched off (0.958 and 1.000 either way). The lateral facts were reachable
// all along, and what kinship supplies is *precision* -- R@1 0.417 to 0.667, MRR
// 0.875 to 1.000, top-1 0.750 to 1.000. That is the same shape the graph channel
// had in Passo 6, where Recall@10 was already 1.000 before expansion and all the
// work was in getting the answer to the top.
//
// The load-bearing case is "the rare pair outranks the common one". Cohorts and
// noise come in the same size in practice -- in the brain above, a class joined
// 23 entities and a `valido true` flag joined 22 -- so no threshold can separate
// them and inverse document frequency has to do the whole job.
